# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and adjust if you named your
# certificate differently.
#
# APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY is the name of the local, free, self-signed macOS
# code-signing certificate used to sign dev builds so the Accessibility
# permission grant survives rebuilds (issue 002). It is read by the Tauri
# CLI at build time (`pnpm tauri build`). See docs/dev-signing.md for how to
# create the certificate and a caveat about `pnpm tauri dev` not picking
# this up yet.
#
# This is a LOCAL, per-machine value — never hardcode a real certificate
# name into committed config.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="JC Grid Manager Dev"
